# SIX CLASSES ARE RETIRED AND GONE, AND EVERY ONE OF THEIR ROWS IS EXACT NOW. THEY ARE NOT
# IN `CLASSES` ANY MORE: A CLASS WITH NO ROWS IS A CLAIM THAT HAS STOPPED BEING TRUE, AND
# `classes_hold()` FAILS A CLASS THAT HAS NONE. EACH STORY IS BELOW, WITH THE READING.

# HI_BIT -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 12, AND **HALF OF THE CLASS WAS TWO DEFECTS**. (i) `vgpr_encode.hi`
# read `fit(set, or(set, X, f), v, f)` -- it OR'd bit 7 in and THEN tested `encoded >= 128`, and
# since ORing 0x80 into an eight-bit value always leaves it >= 128, EVERY `.h` in an eight-bit
# field took dsl.py:196's refusal arm. dsl.py:194-197 tests `encoded` BEFORE the OR. The six
# `_256`/`_300` rows were CPython `128`/`172` against the port's `0`. (ii) THE ROWS READ THE
# WRONG SLOT: `urow(..., Res.v(vgpr_encode(...)))` prints `Res.v`, which IS `0` for a `Bad`, so
# the six `_384`/`_511` rows CPython REFUSES were ALSO `0` -- a RIGHT ANSWER FOR A WRONG REASON
# that read as agreement. `srow(..., enc_text(...))` reads the whole answer, the same slot the
# oracle's `enc` and the neighbouring `vgenc_*`/`afenc_ab_*` rows read. Reading the value slot
# is the SAME SHAPE as `VDSTY_MSG` below, one line over: `Res.v` drops a refusal and `Res.msg`
# drops a value, and neither is the answer `encode` gives.

# ABSENT_OPERAND -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 10, AND IT WAS A DEFECT NOBODY COULD SEE BECAUSE IT WAS
# ZERO. `BitField.set` (:114) opens `if val is None: val = self.default`, so an omitted operand
# is written at its DEFAULT; `fld_encode` NEVER READ `Vf.has`. It did not have to, because every
# fixture that omits an operand spells the omission `Ov.none()` and `Ov.none().off` is 0 -- and
# every default in this file ENCODES to 0 (`s[0]`/`v[0]` sit at their range's low end so :171's
# subtraction is 0; the aligned classes' default is the bare int 0, which :207 accepts). So a
# missing field and a zero field were the same number. MEASURED: `raw_vop2_neg` CPython
# `|0x14060a00`, port `|0x00000000`, and the port's `al_encode` REFUSED `sdst` outright because
# `Ov.none()` is not a `Reg` -- so the walk stopped and every earlier field was thrown away. The
# three fixtures with NO omitted operand (`_all`, `_big`, `_big2`) agreed all along, which is why
# ten rows moved and 1174 rows did not. `VDSTY` is the ONE class whose default does not encode
# (:224 wants a Reg), so it keeps a refusal -- and no fixture omits a vd sty, so nothing here
# measures that arm.

# VDSTY_MSG -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 9, AND IT WAS NOT A DIFFERENT DEFECT FROM HI_BIT, IT WAS THE SAME
# ONE. `vdstyencneg_*` read `Res.msg(vdsty_encode(...))` -- the refusal slot -- while the oracle
# read `enc`, the WHOLE answer. Six rows were answers CPython gives that the port dropped (CPython
# `0`, `0`, `1`, `1`, `127`, `127` against the port's empty string, because `Res.msg` is `""` for
# a `Res`), and three were refusals whose TEXT is already right. `enc_text` is the port's `enc`.
# BOTH CLASSES WERE "THE ROW DID NOT READ WHAT THE CALL RETURNS", and both were one word.

# MOD_MERGE -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 10, AND **THE CAUSE IS NOW ESTABLISHED; IT WAS NOT INSIDE
# `Bool.pick`**. `base.bend:504` is `match c: case False{}: b / case True{}: a`, which is exactly
# how the call read. `mod_merge` put an OUTER `Bool.pick` around the answer with the LITERAL `0`
# as its else arm and `Bool.and(has, U32.is_zero(bits))` as its condition, so it answered 0 for
# every case where `has` is false OR `bits` is nonzero -- i.e. every case worth encoding. CPython's
# `(vals.get(k) or 0) | bits` is `has ? (given | bits) : bits`, because the `or 0` is inert once
# the left side is a U32 (`0 | bits` IS `bits`), which is also the reading that makes
# `mod_merge(2, True{}, 1)` CPython `3` and `mod_merge(0, False{}, 1)` CPython `1`.
# AND A SECOND, INDEPENDENT DEFECT WAS IN THE ROWS, NOT THE DEF: `modmerge_{given}_0_{bits}` --
# THE MIDDLE DIGIT IS `has`, and it is `0` in every one of these rows on BOTH sides, because
# `vals` is a dict (dsl.py:300-307/:334-335) and a value is looked up BY NAME, so "the caller
# supplied it" is not expressible as a value's position. Three port rows passed `True{}` where
# their own NAME says `0`. Both halves are fixed; the second is why `modmerge_2_0_0` was CPython
# `0` against the port's `2` while `modmerge_0_0_*` agreed.

# WALK_IS_VALUES -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 1, AND **THE ORACLE WAS THE SIDE THAT WAS WRONG**. The port's
# `Vf` list carries each value's own field, so the port's list order IS `dsl.py:334-335`'s
# `_fields` order; `raw_ord_swap` walks a TRANSPOSED FIELD LIST. The oracle walked `ORD_FIELDS`
# (unswapped) with the values' ORDER swapped -- and CPython cannot observe a value order at all,
# so the two were not the same fixture. MEASURED on two real `dsl.Inst` subclasses, `first` and
# `second` both at [7:0]:
#     class A(_fields = [first, second]) -> A(first=11, second=22)._raw == 0x16
#     class B(_fields = [second, first]) -> B(first=11, second=22)._raw == 0x0b
#     A(second=22, first=11)._raw == 0x16      # kwargs order is invisible
# The oracle now walks `ORD_FIELDS_SWAP`, which it already declared and never used.

# SLICE_UNSIGNED -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 1. `reg_slice.go` printed `U32.show(start)` where dsl.py:26
# formats the SIGNED `key.start`; `key_text` -- the def that spells a U32's two's complement back,
# and which the INDEX arm beside it already used -- now spells both bounds. `get_slice_neg_start`
# CPython `slice [-1:5] out of bounds for size 512`, port was `slice [4294967295:5] ...`.

# ALIGN_SHIFT -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 18 AND EVERY ONE IS DROPPED, NOT MOVED: `al_shift_of` read
# `U32.sub(Fld.align(f), 1)`, so for `_align = 4` (`dsl.py:219 SRsrcField`) it answered 3 where
# dsl.py:210/:211 shift by `_align.bit_length() - 1 = 2`, and every `afdec_sr_*` came out DOUBLE
# (`afdec_sr_32` was 256,1 against CPython's 128,1). THE FILE ALREADY SAID SO -- the note at
# dsl.bend:870 reads "whose shift is `_align.bit_length() - 1` ... NOT the alignment itself", and
# `ALIGN_SHIFT_2`/`ALIGN_SHIFT_4` at :252-253 ARE THE CORRECT CONSTANTS. THEY WERE DEAD:
# `grep -c` answered 2, their own two definitions and no call site. THE THIRD INSTANCE OF THIS
# FILE'S OWN RECORDED CLASS -- "a def nothing calls is invisible to every other check", the same
# fault its mask defs had. IT IS A MASK-VERSUS-SHIFT CONFLATION AND `al_aligned` SHOWS WHY THE TWO
# LOOK ALIKE: `U32.and(off, align - 1)` IS a mask and IS correct, and the same expression read as a
# SHIFT is wrong. THE CONSTANTS ARE NOW CALLED AND THE 18 ROWS ARE EXACT.

